.TH SWAYDESK-SETTINGS 1 2026-11-25 "swaydesk 0.2.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-settings \- the Swaydesk Settings center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-settings
.RB [ \-\-panel
.IR name ]
.br
.B swaydesk\-settings \-\-about
.SH DESCRIPTION
One window with a panel for each part of the desktop, listed in a sidebar: appearance, displays, keyboard,
mouse and touchpad, power and lock, desktop, default apps, region and about. The About panel shows the
distribution, the kernel, Sway's version, the processor, the memory, the graphics, the disk use of / and the
device name, with a Copy info button for bug reports, Help (when it is installed) and Website. Copy info
copies the same report as
.BR \-\-about :
in English, and without the device name, since it goes into public bug reports. The Desktop
panel turns the session's components and the bar's modules on and off and picks the shortcut profile: it
writes the [enabled] and [enabled.bar] tables and the shortcuts key of
.IR ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml ,
keeping its comments, shows the values that come from
.I /etc/swaydesk/config.toml
and the components that are not installed, and says when each change applies. The Region panel sets the
language (locale, at the next login), the weather city (weather_location) and the holidays country (holidays);
an empty field removes the key, so the default applies again, and a value the config would refuse is not
written. The Power and lock panel sets the idle times (lock_after, screen_off_after and suspend_after, on
battery; Never to 60 minutes) and runs sway\-idle again so they apply at once in the Swaydesk session, or says
swaydesk\-caffeine is missing; with power\-profiles\-daemon running, it also picks the power profile. The Default apps panel sets the web
browser, mail, text editor, images, PDF, video and music apps in
.IR ~/.config/mimeapps.list ,
only the user's layer (the system default, as in
.IR /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list ,
shows as "System default" and is never written), and the file manager and the terminal through the
file_manager and terminal keys of the config. App names follow the config's locale; when it differs from the
session's language, an app translated only by the distribution's language packs shows its untranslated name.
.PP
The Appearance and Displays panels are the pages of the Theme and Displays apps, which stay separate apps with
their own windows (see
.BR swaydesk\-theme\-app (1)
and
.BR swaydesk\-displays (1));
each panel appears only when its app is installed. The Keyboard panel picks the layouts and their order, the
switch key, the repeat delay and rate, and Num Lock at login; Use the system keyboard drops its layouts, so the
system keyboard of 50\-local.conf applies again (the login screen always uses it). The Mouse and touchpad panel
sets the speed, natural scrolling and the left\-handed button, and, with a touchpad, tap to click and disable
while typing; it shows the values Sway applies now. Both panels write only the keys changed there and apply
them at once. The network, Bluetooth and sound panels appear only when their program is installed
(nm\-connection\-editor, blueman\-manager, pavucontrol), and open it. Without it, \fB\-\-panel\fR names the
package to install on that distribution (network\-manager\-gnome and blueman on Debian and Ubuntu;
nm\-connection\-editor and blueman on Arch).
.PP
There is one Settings window: running it again with \fB\-\-panel\fR shows that panel in the open window.
Its menu entry is org.swaydesktop.Settings, with an action for each panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-panel " name"
Open on this panel: appearance (or theme), displays (screens, monitors), keyboard, mouse (touchpad), power
(lock), desktop, default\-apps (apps), region, about, network, bluetooth or sound (audio). For network,
Bluetooth and sound, only the program of the panel is started.
.TP
.B \-\-about
Print the text of Copy info and exit, without a window or a display: what to paste into a bug report. It is
in English and leaves out the device name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The user's settings, written by the Desktop, Region, Power and lock and Default apps panels, which keep its
comments.
.TP
.I /etc/swaydesk/config.toml
The system layer: only its [enabled] table is read, under the user's file; never written.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/80\-input.conf
The keys changed in the Keyboard and Mouse and touchpad panels, read by Sway after 50\-local.conf, so they win
over it. Edits by hand are replaced at the next change in a panel.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mimeapps.list
The default apps of the user; the system's, as in
.IR /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list ,
are only read.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/displays.json
.TQ
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/90\-displays.conf
Written by the Displays panel, as by the Displays app.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the program of an outside panel is not installed or does not start; 2 for an unknown
panel or argument, also when the window is already open (it then stays as it was).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk\-theme\-app (1),
.BR swaydesk\-displays (1),
.BR swaydesk (7)
